Camille,<br />
<br />
Referring Marchwood Asset Management LLC to Enforcement out of examination =
EX-2023-14406. The referral memorandum is attached.<br />
<br />
The substance of the tip is confirmed. From March 2019 through the present =
Marchwood has held standing authority to instruct client custodians to debi=
t advisory fees, and has exercised it, across 431 accounts holding roughly =
$497 million. No surprise examination was obtained for 2019, 2020, 2021 or =
2022. No Form ADV-E was filed for any of those years. Form ADV Part 1 Items=
 9.A.(1)(a) and 9.A.(1)(b) answer "no" in every annual amendment across the=
 period. The compliance manual in force contains no custody procedure at al=
l.<br />
<br />
We also pulled the registrant's filing history. Forms ADV-E were filed on M=
archwood's behalf for calendar years 2011 and 2013 and for no year after th=
at. That tells us surprise examinations were performed in those two years. =
It does not tell us why, and the firm's position is that they were voluntar=
y.<br />
<br />
Two things I could not resolve and want to name rather than bury.<br />
<br />
The firm's current CCO, Renata Sczerbiak, told us the practice predates her=
 and that she was told when she arrived that it had been examined and clear=
ed. She could not produce anything and neither could we. Our record of the =
2011 examination in SENTRY is a summary line reading closed, no further act=
ion, and a two-paragraph closing letter that says the same. On that record =
the firm was examined in 2011 and nothing was required of it.<br />
<br />
Second, this is the same practice on a larger book, which either means we m=
issed it in 2011 or it came back. I cannot tell you which from what is in t=
he system.<br />
<br />
Yolanda Bricenio<br />
Branch Chief, Division of Examinations, Philadelphia Regional Office
